{
 "esm": "1.2.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "WRFCurvature",
  "description": "WRF-ARW's Earth-curvature (metric) momentum terms, SUBROUTINE curvature of dyn_em/module_big_step_utilities_em.F:4175-4469 on its 'normal code' path (map_proj /= 6, not polar), written as instantaneous decoupled tendencies of a single column on the EarthSciDiscretizations column_nonuniform_1d grid. rk_tendency applies them unconditionally, so even the idealized Cartesian em_scm_xy column carries them: du/dt = -u w / a, dv/dt = -v w / a on the layers, and dw/dt = (u^2 + v^2)/a on the interior interfaces (Skamarock et al. 2021, section 2.3; a = the Earth radius, WRF reradius = 1/a). In the reference column the w term is (3^2 + 9^2)/a = 1.4e-5 m/s^2, a few percent of the pressure-gradient-plus-buoyancy tendency, so it is not negligible; PLAN.md 3.1 did not list it. Discretization as in WRF for a horizontally uniform column: w enters the u and v terms as the mean of the two bounding interfaces, and u, v enter the w term linearly interpolated onto the interior interfaces 2..NLEV with the weights w_above/w_below (WRF fzm/fzp); the surface and top interfaces get no term. WRF multiplies the interpolated MASS-COUPLED wind by the interpolated wind; with a constant dry column mass the coupling mass cancels and the product is the square of the interpolated wind. Not transcribed: the vxgm terms (the zonal gradient of the map factor times the wind, plus the tan(latitude) terms of the polar and global-projection branch), identically zero for the uniform map factors of the idealized column, and the general map-factor ratios (all 1 there). Consumer-supplied column fields are rewrite-target ops input_<name>.",
  "license": "MIT",
  "tags": ["wrf", "dynamics", "curvature", "metric-terms", "column"],
  "references": [
   {"citation": "Skamarock, W. C., et al. (2021). A Description of the Advanced Research WRF Model Version 4.3. NCAR/TN-556+STR, section 2.3 (curvature terms).", "doi": "10.5065/1dfh-6p97"},
   {"citation": "WRF v4.8.0 dyn_em/module_big_step_utilities_em.F:4175-4469 (curvature), called from dyn_em/module_em.F:773 (rk_tendency)."}
  ]
 },
 "metaparameters": {
  "NLEV": {"type": "integer", "default": 59, "description": "Number of model layers (WRF kde - 1). Bound into the column grid at the import edge; 59 is the em_scm_xy reference column."}
 },
 "models": {
  "WRFCurvature": {
   "expression_template_imports": [
    {"ref": "${ESD_ROOT}/grids/column_nonuniform_1d/grid.esm", "bindings": {"NLEV": "NLEV"}},
    {"ref": "./column_staggering.esm"}
   ],
   "subsystems": {"wrf": {"ref": "../../../lib/wrf_constants.esm"}},
   "variables": {
    "w_above_in": {"type": "parameter", "units": "1", "shape": ["lev_nodes"], "default": 0.0, "description": "Coupling target (assembly input path): a shaped parameter that receives the interface interpolation weight of the layer above (WRF fnm), from the column geometry through a document-level `coupling.variable_map` (`param_to_var`) when an assembly's mount-edge template library lowers `input_w_above` to this parameter. Unused in the component's own inline tests, which lower `input_w_above` to a dumped profile."},
    "w_below_in": {"type": "parameter", "units": "1", "shape": ["lev_nodes"], "default": 0.0, "description": "Coupling target (assembly input path): a shaped parameter that receives the interface interpolation weight of the layer below (WRF fnp), from the column geometry through a document-level `coupling.variable_map` (`param_to_var`) when an assembly's mount-edge template library lowers `input_w_below` to this parameter. Unused in the component's own inline tests, which lower `input_w_below` to a dumped profile."},
    "u_in": {"type": "parameter", "units": "m/s", "shape": ["lev"], "default": 0.0, "description": "Coupling target (assembly input path): a shaped parameter that receives the layer zonal wind u from the EqWeather-SCM state document's ODE state (couplings/eqweather_scm_dynamics.esm) through a document-level `coupling.variable_map` (`param_to_var`), when that document's mount-edge library couplings/tests/scmstate_couple_cur_inputs.esm lowers `input_u` to it. Unused in the component's own inline tests, which lower `input_u` to a dumped profile instead."},
    "v_in": {"type": "parameter", "units": "m/s", "shape": ["lev"], "default": 0.0, "description": "Coupling target (assembly input path): a shaped parameter that receives the layer meridional wind v from the EqWeather-SCM state document's ODE state (couplings/eqweather_scm_dynamics.esm) through a document-level `coupling.variable_map` (`param_to_var`), when that document's mount-edge library couplings/tests/scmstate_couple_cur_inputs.esm lowers `input_v` to it. Unused in the component's own inline tests, which lower `input_v` to a dumped profile instead."},
    "w_in": {"type": "parameter", "units": "m/s", "shape": ["lev_nodes"], "default": 0.0, "description": "Coupling target (assembly input path): a shaped parameter that receives the interface vertical velocity w from the EqWeather-SCM state document's ODE state (couplings/eqweather_scm_dynamics.esm) through a document-level `coupling.variable_map` (`param_to_var`), when that document's mount-edge library couplings/tests/scmstate_couple_cur_inputs.esm lowers `input_w` to it. Unused in the component's own inline tests, which lower `input_w` to a dumped profile instead."},
    "u": {"type": "unknown", "units": "m/s", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Zonal wind on the layers, through `input_u`."},
    "v": {"type": "unknown", "units": "m/s", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Meridional wind on the layers, through `input_v`."},
    "w": {"type": "unknown", "units": "m/s", "shape": ["lev_nodes"], "description": "Vertical velocity on the interfaces, through `input_w`."},
    "w_above": {"type": "unknown", "units": "1", "shape": ["lev_nodes"], "description": "Interpolation weight of the layer above each interior interface (WRF fnm), through `input_w_above`."},
    "w_below": {"type": "unknown", "units": "1", "shape": ["lev_nodes"], "description": "Interpolation weight of the layer below each interior interface (WRF fnp), through `input_w_below`."},
    "w_c": {"type": "unknown", "units": "m/s", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Vertical velocity at the layers, the mean of the two bounding interfaces."},
    "u_w": {"type": "unknown", "units": "m/s", "shape": ["lev_nodes"], "description": "Zonal wind on the interior interfaces; 0 on the faces."},
    "v_w": {"type": "unknown", "units": "m/s", "shape": ["lev_nodes"], "description": "Meridional wind on the interior interfaces; 0 on the faces."},
    "du_dt": {"type": "unknown", "units": "m/s^2", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Curvature tendency of u, -u w / a."},
    "dv_dt": {"type": "unknown", "units": "m/s^2", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Curvature tendency of v, -v w / a."},
    "dw_dt": {"type": "unknown", "units": "m/s^2", "shape": ["lev_nodes"], "description": "Curvature tendency of w, (u^2 + v^2)/a; 0 on the surface and top interfaces."}
   },
   "equations": [
    {"lhs": "u", "rhs": {"op": "input_u", "args": []}},
    {"lhs": "v", "rhs": {"op": "input_v", "args": []}},
    {"lhs": "w", "rhs": {"op": "input_w", "args": []}},
    {"lhs": "w_above", "rhs": {"op": "input_w_above", "args": []}},
    {"lhs": "w_below", "rhs": {"op": "input_w_below", "args": []}},
    {"lhs": "w_c", "rhs": {"op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "column_cell_center", "bindings": {"ze": "w"}}},
    {"lhs": "u_w", "rhs": {"op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "interpolate_to_interfaces", "bindings": {"f": "u", "wa": "w_above", "wb": "w_below"}}},
    {"lhs": "v_w", "rhs": {"op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "interpolate_to_interfaces", "bindings": {"f": "v", "wa": "w_above", "wb": "w_below"}}},
    {"lhs": "du_dt", "rhs": {"op": "*", "args": [{"op": "-", "args": ["wrf.reradius"]}, "u", "w_c"]}},
    {"lhs": "dv_dt", "rhs": {"op": "*", "args": [{"op": "-", "args": ["wrf.reradius"]}, "v", "w_c"]}},
    {"lhs": "dw_dt", "rhs": {"op": "*", "args": ["wrf.reradius", {"op": "+", "args": [{"op": "^", "args": ["u_w", 2]}, {"op": "^", "args": ["v_w", 2]}]}]}}
   ],
   "tests": [
     {
       "id": "curvature_step60",
       "description": "Reference: WRF 4.8 em_scm_xy single-column run (GNU gfortran 13.3 REAL*4 build, dt = 60 s, damp_opt = 2 dampcoef = 0.003 zdamp = 5000 m, pert_coriolis = .true., use_theta_m = 1, hybrid_opt = 0; data/eqwefic/scm_dyn, the scm_ref namelist re-run with the instrumented binary) dumped by the ctessum-claude/WRF fork, branch earthsciml-instrumented, commit 83347b2 (dyn_em/module_em.F rk_tendency, rk_step 1 of the step; module_esm_dump), merged with the same step's radiation subassembly dump and the wrfout eta grid by tools/merge_dumps.py into data/eqwefic/dumps/dyn_column/esm_dump_dyn_suite_<step>.json. The rebuilt binary reproduces the archived scm_ref radiation subassembly dumps bit for bit (all but the three B9 variables). The column is horizontally uniform (u, v identical in the two tile columns, ww = 0, all map factors 1, c1 = 1, c2 = 0). Expected tendencies are the dumped mass-coupled increments of the named routine divided by the coupling mass of their grid point (muu, muv, mut), i.e. the instantaneous decoupled rate at the time-level-n state; references are single precision, so tolerances follow the rel 1e-5 real32 convention, with absolute Linf bounds on whole profiles where values pass through zero. Routine: curvature, normal-code branch (dyn_em/module_big_step_utilities_em.F:4175-4469); the vxgm map-factor-gradient terms are identically zero in this column. The eta interpolation weights are the dumped fnm/fnp. Measured residual over the three regimes (zero tolerance): Linf <= 1.2e-11 m/s^2 in du_dt and <= 5.5e-12 in dv_dt (values <= 5e-10, <= 9e-10), <= 2.1e-11 in dw_dt (values 1.41e-5, <= 1.5e-6 relative). These are NOT transcription errors but the resolution of the reference: the dump records each routine's contribution as the difference of the single-precision tendency array across the call, and curvature is added onto a tendency that already holds the Coriolis (and, for w, the pressure-gradient-plus-buoyancy) term of O(40) in mass-coupled units, so a ~3e-5 coupled increment is quantized to one ulp of 40, 3.8e-6, i.e. 4.8e-11 m/s^2 after dividing by mu = 79265 Pa (the level-1 u increment, ~1e-6 coupled, even rounds to exactly 0). Linf bounds are therefore set at that quantization limit, abs 5e-11 m/s^2; the w term, far above it, is also asserted pointwise at rel 1e-5. A sign error or a missing term moves each tendency by its full value (up to 9e-10 in u and v, 1.4e-5 in w) and fails. Regime: step 60 (t = 1 h, early afternoon, convective boundary layer).",
       "parameter_overrides": {},
